    "The control tensor very likely has few to no all zero axes whereas the experiment evidently does.  The role of chiseling is to recover such anamolies without knowing ahead of time.  So we now randomize the experiment so as to obscure this data.  Note that the randomization applies random bases change so the original coordinates.  \n",
    "\n",
    "It should now be much less obvious that the control and experminet are any different."
   ]
