    "If you attempt to display `Ξ` you may discover `randomize` has switched the internal representation of tensors the `ITensor` format.  In fact this why we are able to apply a **list** (Julia `Vector` types) of matrices to `Δ` without specifying what side to multiply on.  The order is immaterial, for example `Xs*Δ` is allowable as well.  This is in contrast to matrix multiplication where sides indicate the axis of application.  `ITensors` uses internal markers to permit the correct application across multiple axes.\n",
    "\n",
    "To see the contents in its original array format you can use `asarray(Δ)`."
   ]
